# Did I Do It? Habits Tracker Privacy Policy
Effective Date: 04-May-2026

# 1. Overview
Did I Do It? (“the App”) is designed to help you track what you’ve done and when. Your privacy is important, and this policy explains what data is collected, how it is used, and your rights.

# 2. Data We Collect
a) Information You Provide

The App stores the information you enter, including:

Habit names Log entries (timestamps of when you record actions) Scheduling preferences (e.g. daily, weekly, or interval settings)

This data is used solely to provide the App’s functionality.

b) Automatically Collected Data

The App does not collect personal information such as:

Your name Email address Location Contacts

# 3. How Your Data Is Used
Your data is used only to:

Display your habits and logs Provide timing awareness and reminders Improve your experience within the App

Your data is not sold, shared, or used for advertising purposes.

# 4. Data Storage
By default:

Your data is stored locally on your device

If you delete the App, your data may be deleted as well.

# 5. Third-Party Services
The App does not use third-party services that collect personal data.

# 6. Data Security
We take reasonable steps to protect your data. However, no method of storage or transmission is 100% secure.

# 7. Your Choices
You can:

Edit or delete your data at any time within the App Delete all data by uninstalling the App

# 8. Children’s Privacy
The App is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect personal data from children.

# 9. Changes to This Policy
This policy may be updated from time to time. Updates will be reflected with a new “Effective Date.”

